course: dictionary
lesson: 9235
title: Soon and sooner
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Soon is a small word that tells you when something happens. Its main meaning is in a short time from now or from then. «See you soon» means you will meet again before long. To check, swap in your meaning: "See you in a short time" still makes sense.
explain: Soon can also mean early or quickly, and the context tells you which meaning you have. «Don't speak too soon» means do not speak before you know the facts. The warning is the clue: the speaker is too early.
explain: Sooner is the comparing form, and it can mean rather. «I would sooner walk than take the bus» means I would prefer to walk. The word than tells you that two choices are being compared.
fact: Soon means in a short time from now or from then.
fact: «Get well soon» means that you hope the person will get better in a short time.
fact: «As soon as» means right at the moment when, as in «as soon as possible».
fact: «Sooner or later» means some time, for sure, and «the sooner the better» means it is best if it happens quickly.
fact: Soon is an adverb, and its comparing forms are sooner and soonest.
exercise: «See you soon» means what? | Very loudly | Yesterday | Never again | *In a short time
exercise: In «Soon it began to rain», which word moves the story ahead? | rain | to | began | *Soon
exercise: Mia says «I would sooner walk than take the bus». What does sooner mean here? | *Would rather | More tired | Later in the day | Faster than a bus
test: «Don't speak too soon» means: | *Don't speak before you know the facts | Speak at once, with no thought | Speak loudly | Never speak at all
test: Which phrase means right at the moment when? | *as soon as | the sooner the better | get well soon | sooner or later
exam: In «and soon the Rat is scribbling poetry», what does soon show? | *The Rat starts writing poetry in a short time | The Rat is very old | The Rat is scribbling in the rain | The Rat stops writing for good
